        "original_id": "d7325c88-ec28-5225-9ce9-3759d7638ae4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Symbolic Manipulation Program (SMP), A New Kind of Science\n- People: Chris A. Cole, Stephen Wolfram, Geoffrey C. Fox, Jeffrey M. Greif, Eric D. Mjolsness, Larry J. Romans, Timothy Shaw, Anthony E. Terrano\n- Organizations: Caltech, Caltech physics department\n- Topics: computer algebra systems\n\nFacts:\n- Circa 1979, Chris A. Cole and Stephen Wolfram designed the Symbolic Manipulation Program, usually called SMP, as a computer algebra system at Caltech.\n- The Caltech physics department initially developed SMP under Stephen Wolfram's leadership with contributions from Geoffrey C. Fox, Jeffrey M. Greif, Eric D. Mjolsness, Larry J. Romans, Timothy Shaw, and Anthony E. Terrano.\n- Stephen Wolfram is the author of the book \"A New Kind of Science.\"",
